  "worked_solution": "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ -k & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =(k-1)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -4k+4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4k-4 \\\\ -4k+4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-16=4k-4, \\\\ -4k+4=-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $k$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-12=4k\\,\u27f9\\,k=-3.\n$$\n\nThe second equation is true for any value of $k.$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $k=-3.$",
